userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: Electrophilic bromination of benzene proceeds through a high-energy cationic intermediate and two activation barriers, with substitution favored because it restores aromaticity and ends downhill while addition would end uphill.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): Both pathways share the same high-energy intermediate, but substitution wins because it restores aromaticity and ends lower in energy, while addition destroys aromaticity and ends uphill.
DEMO STEPS: 6 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

